zero_assessment: the four answers are kept apart
  PASS  zero before the event is ALREADY_ZERO, not 'reached zero'
  PASS  ALREADY_ZERO reports no latency at all
  PASS  a real extinction is CONFIRMED_ZERO
  PASS  first contact is at the event, within one sample
  PASS  the confirmed time is min_confirm_s after first contact
  PASS  the hold really was at least min_confirm_s
  PASS  a single sample inside the tolerance is UNCONFIRMED_ZERO, not zero
  PASS  the unconfirmed hold is shorter than min_confirm_s
  PASS  a single-sample touch is not marked as truncated by the window
  PASS  a window that ends before the hold can be confirmed is UNCONFIRMED_ZERO
  PASS  and it is flagged as truncated by the window, not as a negative result
  PASS  never inside the tolerance is NOT_OBSERVED
  PASS  an empty window is NO_DATA, not zero
  PASS  NO_DATA reports zero samples
  PASS  no sample before the event is NO_BASELINE_BEFORE_EVENT
recovery_assessment: coming back must also be held
  PASS  a sustained return is CONFIRMED_RECOVERY
  PASS  recovery latency is measured from the event
  PASS  the recovered level is compared against the reference
  PASS  a single sample out of the tolerance is not a recovery
first_change_descriptive: ripple is not a reaction
